## Reproduction
Important: open the StackBlitz preview in a separate browser tab. React DevTools cannot profile the embedded StackBlitz iframe.

## Steps to reproduce

1. Open the StackBlitz project above.
2. Open its preview in a separate tab.
3. Open React Developer Tools → **Profiler**.
4. In Profiler settings, enable **Record why each component rendered while profiling**.
5. Start a profiling recording.
6. Type one character into the input.
7. Stop the recording.

## Actual behavior

React DevTools reports:

```text
React instrumentation encountered an error:
Error: Unknown Fiber. Needs to be a function component to inspect hooks.
    at inspectHooksOfFiberImpl (installHook.js)
    at inspectHooksOfFiber (installHook.js)
    at inspectHooks (installHook.js)
    at recordProfilingDurations (installHook.js)
    at updateFiberRecursively (installHook.js)
```

The error is triggered by a controlled component implemented as `memo(forwardRef(...))` when its parent re-renders and supplies a new inline `onChange` callback.

Typing changes the controlled value and re-renders the memoized forward-ref input with changed props. This triggers the DevTools instrumentation error.

## Expected behavior

The Profiler should record render reasons without throwing an instrumentation error.

## Minimal reproduction shape

```jsx
const ControlledMemoInput = memo(
    forwardRef(function ControlledMemoInput(
        { onChange, value },
        forwardedRef
    ) {
        const context = useContext(InputContext);
        const inputRef = useRef(null);
        const isFilled = useMemo(() => value.length > 0, [value]);

        useEffect(() => {
            if (typeof forwardedRef === "function") {
                forwardedRef(inputRef.current);
            }
        }, [forwardedRef]);

        return (
            <input
                ref={inputRef}
                disabled={context.disabled}
                onChange={onChange}
                value={value}
                data-filled={isFilled}
            />
        );
    })
);

function App() {
    const [value, setValue] = useState("");
    const [renderRevision, setRenderRevision] = useState(0);

    useEffect(() => {
        setRenderRevision(1);
    }, []);

    return (
        <ControlledMemoInput
            value={value}
            onChange={(event) => setValue(event.target.value)}
        />
    );
}
```

## Investigation

The failure appears to be inside React DevTools’ render-change inspection.

The profiler’s change-description path handles `MemoComponent` fibers and calls `inspectHooks`, but `inspectHooksOfFiberImpl` rejects the outer memo fiber with:

```text
Unknown Fiber. Needs to be a function component to inspect hooks.
```

The relevant component is a `memo(forwardRef(...))` Fiber, not a plain function component, simple memo component, or plain forward-ref component.

## Workaround

Disable **Record why each component rendered while profiling**. Normal profiling continues to work, but render-reason information is unavailable.

